flowchart TD
    REQ([Incoming Request]) --> CORS{OPTIONS?}
    CORS -->|Yes| CORSOK[204 CORS preflight]
    CORS -->|No| METHOD{HTTP Method}

    %% ── GET ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    METHOD -->|GET| G1[Read ?slug from query params]
    G1 --> G2[Query users table\nWHERE clientName = slug]
    G2 --> G3{linear_slug\nfound?}
    G3 -->|No| G4[400 / 404 error]
    G3 -->|Yes| G5[("Supabase DB")]
    G5 -->|getIssueMetricsByCustomerId| G6[issue_metrics]
    G5 -->|getCycleMetricsByCustomerId| G7[cycle_metrics]
    G6 & G7 --> G8[Return issue_metrics\n+ cycle_metrics JSON]

    %% ── PUT ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    METHOD -->|PUT| P1[Read linear_slug\nfrom request body]
    P1 --> P2[getProjectIdsBySlug\nfrom Supabase]
    P2 --> P3{Projects\nfound?}
    P3 -->|No| P4[404 error]
    P3 -->|Yes| P5[fetchProjectDetails\nLinear API]
    P5 --> P6[Scan issues → find\nactive cycles per project]
    P6 --> P7[resolveCycleIssues\nfetch each unique cycle once\ngroup issues by project.id]
    P7 --> P8[buildIssueMetrics]
    P8 --> P9[Return status counts\nby project JSON]

    %% ── POST / Cron ──────────────────────────────────────
    %% DORA metrics run on their own cron (POST /functions/v1/dora,
    %% method: "allCustomers") — decoupled from this cron so a slow/
    %% rate-limited GitHub run never delays or times out Linear metrics.
    METHOD -->|POST / Cron| C1[getAllCustomers\nfrom Supabase]
    C1 --> C2[For each customer\nwith linear_projects]
    C2 --> C3[fetchProjectDetails\nLinear API]
    C3 --> C4[Scan issues → find\nactive cycles per project]
    C4 --> C5[resolveCycleIssues\nfetch unique cycles\ngroup by project.id]
    C5 --> C6[buildIssueMetrics\n+ buildCycleMetrics]
    C6 --> C7[("Supabase DB")]
    C7 -->|upsertIssueMetrics| C8[issue_metrics table]
    C7 -->|upsertCycleMetrics| C9[cycle_metrics table]
    C8 & C9 --> C2
    C2 -->|All customers done| DONE([Return ok: true])
